## Capsule (Capsa)

This project's management truth is stored as a conforming **Capsa
capsule** at `.capsa/` (Capsa 0.2.0). aims is the active
self-maintenance layer over that passive capsule.

- **Decisions (ADRs)** → `.capsa/decisions/NNNN-slug.md`. Proposed
  automatically during plan close-out (the implementation session decides
  per a confidence rule; see `/plan`). For ad-hoc decisions outside a
  plan, write one directly with `status: proposed`. Decisions are
  append-only — to change one, write a new decision that supersedes it
  (`supersedes:` / `superseded_by:` pointers).
- **Plans** → `.capsa/plans/NNNN-slug.md` (frontmatter `status:`).
- **Insights (memory)** → `.capsa/insights/{code,dev,design}/`. Code
  insights carry `code_globs`; freshness is the `updated:` date.
- **Charter** → `.capsa/charter.md`; manifest → `.capsa/capsule.yaml`.

The vendored `validator/validate.py` checks conformance (stdlib only).

## Workflow

Two slash commands only:

- `/plan <task>` — non-trivial change. Read-only planning, a durable
  `status: draft` plan record in `.capsa/plans/`, then implementation,
  then inline close-out (verify, auto-ADR, mark completed, insight
  consolidation).
- `/install-on <path>` — install or re-install aims (idempotent).

Everything else (bug-fix patches, refactors with obvious scope,
mechanical edits, ad-hoc questions): just do the work inline.

## Models policy

- Planning + plan close-out → **Opus** (auto via slash command frontmatter).
- Implementation → any model — switch with `/model <name>` per preference.

## Hooks

**aims hooks inform; they never block.** There is no planning lock and no
`block` mode — a hook's only effect is to inject **factual** context
(`additionalContext`), never to stop an edit (ADR-0020). Discipline is
achieved by awareness:

- `UserPromptSubmit` injects the relevant insight and, for an actionable
  prompt, a factual planning-convention note.
- `PreToolUse` (`pre-write`) never blocks; on the first source edit of a
  session with no in-progress plan it injects the planning convention once.
- `PostToolUse` (`post-edit-marker`) names any insight whose `code_globs`
  cover the edited file (its staleness is then computed from `updated:` vs
  git), and stamps an advisory marker outside the capsule. Concurrency: same
  session refreshes silently; another session's marker older than
  `AIMS_NODE_LOCK_STALE_SEC` (default 3600s) is taken over; a fresher one is
  reported as a possible concurrent edit (ask the user before updating).

Injected text MUST be factual, never imperative ("CRITICAL: do X").

## Insights (memory)

The capsule carries a code-anchored memory layer under
`.capsa/insights/`. Each code insight names the files it documents via
`code_globs` and is a NAVIGATOR over the code and decisions — never a copy.

- Insights are bootstrapped by `/install-on` (Phase 5) — a fresh install
  runs a cold-start scan; re-install only augments (adds insights for
  newly-discovered code areas; never overwrites existing bodies).
- **Staleness is computed, not stored** (Capsa §1.4): an insight is stale
  when a file in its `code_globs` changed after its `updated:` date. The
  `PostToolUse` marker hook surfaces this after every Edit/Write; the
  `Stop` hook consolidates stale insights in-band (ADR-0009) when the
  throttle trips (5 stale OR 30 min since last consolidation). Consolidation
  appends a dated delta and bumps `updated:`, clearing the staleness.
- Plan close-out (inline at end of `/plan` implementation) also forces
  consolidation of insights touched by the plan.
- To browse: `ls .capsa/insights/**` or read the charter for orientation.

Project conventions (build/test, models, hooks, layout) stay in CLAUDE.md;
the charter (`.capsa/charter.md`) is the capsule's own summary of them.
